{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jwt9bFNYzH5uHFgEHM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the email, at about 150 words:\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your own cleaner, and $99 to come back\n\nHi [First name],\n\nWhen customers leave Brightway, they tell us two things: price, and too often a different cleaner showing up. You were right about the second, and we've fixed it.\n\nEvery customer now has their own regular cleaner, plus a named backup for sick days and holidays. If your cleaner is ever out, you'll know who's coming instead.\n\nOn price: an every-other-week cleaning for a 3-bedroom home is $165 with us, and we can't match the $140 apps. Here's why. Our cleaners are employees, not contractors, and every visit is insured. Many app services in our area use contractors and don't insure the visit.\n\nCome back for $99 on your first cleaning, then $165 after that. No contract, and you can cancel any time. This offer ends December 31.\n\nReply to this email or call 555-0164 to book.\n\nLisa Grant\nOwner, Brightway Home Cleaning\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes on the wording:\n- The opening speaks about customers in general, so it doesn't claim this particular person left over price. That's because the email goes to all 64, and their reasons differ.\n- I didn't mention cleaners staying longer. Seven left last year, so that claim wouldn't be safe yet.\n- The line about insurance is limited to \"many app services in our area.\" If anyone checks, that's easier to defend than a claim about all of them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":9862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":800},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"contex